content.explanation:
Allure integrates seamlessly with JUnit 5, providing both annotations and programmatic APIs for rich reporting.

**Maven Dependencies**:

```xml
<dependency>
    <groupId>io.qameta.allure</groupId>
    <artifactId>allure-junit5</artifactId>
    <version>2.27.0</version>
    <scope>test</scope>
</dependency>
```

**Gradle Dependencies**:

```groovy
testImplementation 'io.qameta.allure:allure-junit5:2.27.0'
```

**Allure CLI Installation**:

```bash
# macOS
brew install allure

# Windows (with Scoop)
scoop install allure

# Linux
sudo apt-add-repository ppa:qameta/allure
sudo apt-get update
sudo apt-get install allure

# Or download manually from GitHub
```

**Configuration File (allure.properties)**:

```properties
allure.results.directory=target/allure-results
allure.link.issue.pattern=https://jira.example.com/browse/{}
allure.link.tms.pattern=https://testcase.example.com/{}
```

**Basic Test Example**:

```java
import io.qameta.allure.*;
import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;

@Epic("Payment Processing")
@Feature("Credit Card Payments")
public class PaymentTests {

    @Test
    @Story("Successful Payment")
    @Severity(SeverityLevel.CRITICAL)
    @Description("Test that valid credit card payment succeeds")
    @Link(name = "Requirements", url = "https://docs.example.com/req-123")
    @Issue("PAY-456")
    @TmsLink("TC-789")
    public void testValidPayment() {
        // Test code here
    }
}
```

**Generate Report**:

```bash
# Run tests
mvn clean test

# Generate and open report
allure serve target/allure-results

# Generate static report
allure generate target/allure-results --clean -o allure-report
```

Allure integrates with Jest through the jest-allure2 reporter or allure-js-commons.

**Installation**:

```bash
npm install --save-dev jest-allure2
# or
npm install --save-dev allure-js-commons
```

**Jest Configuration (jest.config.js)**:

```javascript
module.exports = {
  reporters: [
    'default',
    ['jest-allure2', {
      resultsDir: './allure-results'
    }]
  ]
};
```

**Basic Test Example**:

```javascript
describe('Payment Processing', () => {
  beforeEach(() => {
    reporter
      .epic('Payment Processing')
      .feature('Credit Card Payments');
  });

  test('Successful payment', async () => {
    await reporter
      .story('Successful Payment')
      .severity('critical')
      .description('Test that valid credit card payment succeeds')
      .link('https://docs.example.com/req-123', 'Requirements')
      .issue('PAY-456')
      .tms('TC-789')
      .startStep('Create payment request');

    const payload = { amount: 1000, card: '4111111111111111' };

    await reporter.endStep();
    await reporter.startStep('Send payment API request');

    const response = await request.post('/api/payments').send(payload);

    await reporter.endStep();
    await reporter.startStep('Verify response');

    expect(response.status).toBe(200);

    await reporter.attach('Response Body', JSON.stringify(response.body), 'application/json');
    await reporter.endStep();
  });
});
```

**Run Tests**:

```bash
npm test -- --testResultsProcessor=jest-allure2
allure serve ./allure-results
```

