content.explanation:
Allure can automatically generate links using patterns, saving annotation repetition.

**allure.properties**:

```properties
# JIRA integration
allure.link.issue.pattern=https://jira.example.com/browse/{}
allure.link.tms.pattern=https://testrail.example.com/index.php?/cases/view/{}

# GitHub integration
allure.link.issue.pattern=https://github.com/org/repo/issues/{}

# Custom link types
allure.link.mypattern.pattern=https://custom.tool.com/{}
```

**Usage with Patterns**:

```java
// This will automatically generate: https://jira.example.com/browse/PAY-123
@Issue("PAY-123")

// This will generate: https://testrail.example.com/index.php?/cases/view/456
@TmsLink("456")

// Custom pattern usage
@Link(type = "mypattern", value = "doc-789")
```

**Benefits of Traceability**:
- **Context**: Anyone can see why a test exists
- **Debugging**: Jump directly to related issues
- **Compliance**: Demonstrate requirements coverage
- **Audit**: Track test-to-requirement relationships

**Integration Examples**:

| Tool | Pattern | Example |
|------|---------|---------|
| Jira | https://jira.company.com/browse/{} | @Issue("PROJ-123") |
| GitHub | https://github.com/org/repo/issues/{} | @Issue("42") |
| TestRail | https://testrail.company.com/index.php?/cases/view/{} | @TmsLink("1234") |
| Confluence | https://wiki.company.com/display/{} | @Link(type="docs", value="PROJ") |

